<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Church of the East</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nestorian Christian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Church of the East is an ancient Christian church centred in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, often called Nestorian. Its missionaries spread its faith across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> in 635, as recorded on the famous Nestorian Stele.</p></div>
